nning sequence in Column E (preventing the upward expansion). Crucially, this move also fills the gap between White\'s stones at D4 and F4, creating a White Open 3 (D4-E4-F4). This is a "Sente" move, meaning it forces Black to defend against White\'s new threat, buying White time and neutralizing Black\'s initiative.\n\nReason: E4 is the only move that simultaneously defends against Black\'s lethal vertical expansion and creates a strong counter-threat (Open 3) for White. Blocking elsewhere (like E8) would allow Black to play E4 and generate overlapping threats (double fours) that would be impossible to stop.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "E", "row": 4}'}
